Catch-up, style recalculation (09:15Z):

1. Platform section fix (PR-002, which you accepted at 08:07Z). It cuts style work at the moment the platform section switches on. In Chrome it is checked to animate and draw like today's build. On the real iPhone we confirmed the cost it targets: two nested layouts at that switch. Still to do: one iPhone check with Safari's own timeline (T-011), then a final review, then it lands. It is 4th in the phone queue:
   (1) PR-001 block B, running now;
   (2) the PR-003 check of your pick, option A;
   (3) the fling test for the page-middle fix below;
   (4) T-011.
   Rough estimate: it starts in about 1.5-2 hours.
2. The middle of the page (y about 2990). Earlier phone checks showed that cutting the platform switch alone moves part of its cost to the next big frame, around y 2990. The page-middle fix (fwreskip) addresses that: the "people" section is set aside while it can't be seen and redrawn after you pause, not mid-fling. Simulator checks are running now, and its phone fling test is (3) above. Note: since recordings stopped (T-018), that test can no longer check one thing on the phone, whether the people section shows up late during a fast fling. It will say so in its result.
3. All figures so far are observations from our own tests. Timing claims stay paused, except for the tests you allowed.
Nothing is waiting on you here. I'll post in this thread when T-011 starts and when it has a result.
